"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pair, as every tour does. nil below three vertices.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A move’s gain is formed as (d(a, b) + d(c, e)) − (d(a, c) + d(b, e)), and the scan stops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when no move gains anything. With floating-point weights, rounding decides which moves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gain."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is complete; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour.vertices"},{"text":" lists every vertex of the graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly once; no weight is NaN or infinite; the sum of any two weights fits in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition","style":"note"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n²) per improving move."}]}],"name":"Complexity","style":"note"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"code":"tour","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" improved by 2-opt to a 2-optimal tour."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/twoopttour(improving:weight:)"]}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/TwoOpt.swift#L135","fileName":"TwoOpt.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE10twoOptTour9improving6weight5Walks5CycleVy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgAP_qd__AOXEts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"twoOptTour"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"improving"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typ